(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_biologicalclassification=[{id:"neet-2026r-q099",pn:99,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Bacterial shapes",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
A. Spherical \u2014 I. Vibrio
B. Rod \u2014 II. Cocci
C. Comma \u2014 III. Spirilla
D. Spirillum \u2014 IV. Bacilli
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV","A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III","A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III","A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV"],c:2,s:`Bacteria are grouped into four categories by shape.
Spherical \u2192 Coccus.
Rod-shaped \u2192 Bacillus.
Comma-shaped \u2192 Vibrio.
Spiral \u2192 Spirillum.`},{id:"neet-2026-q121",pn:121,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Five kingdom classification",q:`The main criteria used for Five Kingdom Classification proposed By R.H. Whittaker (1969) included:
A. Cell structure
B. Body organization
C. Presence of flagellum
D. Reproduction
E. Phylogenetic relationships
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A, B, D and E only","A, B, C, D and E","A, B and E only","B, C and D only"],c:0,s:`The main criteria for five kingdom classification by Whittaker include cell structure, body organisation, mode of nutrition, reproduction and phylogenetic relationships.
Of the listed items, A, B, D and E match.
Presence of flagellum is not a criterion.
Note: Printed solution also lists mode of nutrition, which is not among A-E; printed answer kept.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q123",pn:123,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Lichens",q:"Symbiotic association between fungi and algae are called ________.",o:["sponges","mycorrhiza","chrysophytes","lichens"],c:3,s:`Lichens are symbiotic (mutually useful) associations between algae and fungi.
Mycorrhiza are associations between fungi and roots of higher plants.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q132",pn:132,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Prokaryotes",q:"Which of the following is not a prokaryote?",o:["Blue green algae","Mycoplasma","Fungi","Bacteria"],c:2,s:`Prokaryotic cells are found in bacteria, blue-green algae, Mycoplasma and PPLO.
Fungi are eukaryotic organisms.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q135",pn:135,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Viruses, viroids and prions",q:"Mad cow disease is caused by _______.",o:["viroids","Aspergillus sp.","Mycoplasma sp.","prions"],c:3,s:"Mad cow disease is caused by prions."},{id:"neet-2025-q132",pn:132,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Whittaker five kingdoms",q:`Each of the following characteristics represent a Kingdom proposed by Whittaker. Arrange the following in increasing order of complexity of body organization.
A. Multicellular heterotrophs with cell wall made of chitin.
B. Heterotrophs with tissue/organ/organ system level of body organization.
C. Prokaryotes with cell wall made of polysaccharides and amino acids.
D. Eukaryotic autotrophs with tissue/organ level of body organization.
E. Eukaryotes with cellular body organization.
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A, C, E, B, D","C, E, A, D, B","A, C, E, D, B","C, E, A, B, D"],c:1,s:`Increasing complexity of body organisation in Whittaker's kingdoms:
C. Monera: prokaryotes with cell wall of polysaccharide.
E. Protista: unicellular eukaryotes.
A. Fungi: multicellular heterotrophs with cell wall of chitin.
D. Plantae: eukaryotic autotrophs with tissue body organisation.
B. Animalia: heterotrophs with tissue/organ/system body organisation.
Correct sequence is C, E, A, D, B.`},{id:"neet-2024-q110",pn:110,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Classification of fungi",q:"Which one of the following is not a criterion for classification of fungi?",o:["Mode of spore formation","Fruiting body","Morphology of mycelium","Mode of nutrition"],c:3,s:`Fungi are divided into classes on the basis of the morphology of the mycelium, the mode of spore formation and the fruiting bodies.
Mode of nutrition is not used, so it is the answer.`},{id:"neet-2024-q117",pn:117,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Fungi examples",q:`Match List I with List II
A. Rhizopus \u2014 I. Mushroom
B. Ustilago \u2014 II. Smut fungus
C. Puccinia \u2014 III. Bread mould
D. Agaricus \u2014 IV. Rust fungus
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV","A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I","A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV"],c:2,s:`Rhizopus is a bread mould.
Ustilago is a smut fungus.
Puccinia is a rust fungus.
Agaricus is commonly called a mushroom.
So: A-III, B-II, C-IV, D-I.`},{id:"neet-2022-q153",pn:153,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Asexual spores in fungi",q:"Identify the asexual reproductive structure associated with Penicillium :",o:["Conidia","Gemmules","Buds","Zoospores"],c:0,s:`Penicillium reproduces asexually by conidia.
Gemmules are made in sponges.
Buds are made in Hydra.
Zoospores are made in Chlamydomonas.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q169",pn:169,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Viruses, viroids and prions",q:"Mad cow disease in cattle and Cr Jacob disease in humans are due to infection by __________.",o:["Prion","Bacterium","Virus","Viroid"],c:0,s:`Mad cow disease and Creutzfeldt-Jakob disease are caused by prions.
Prions are abnormally folded proteins.`},{id:"neet-2022-q170",pn:170,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Mycoplasma",q:`Given below are two statements :
Statement I : Mycoplasma can pass through less than 1 micron filter size.
Statement II : Mycoplasma are bacteria with cell wall.
In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below`,o:["Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect","Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect","Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct","Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"],c:1,s:`Mycoplasma are the smallest cells, only about 0.3 \u03BCm long, so they pass through filters of less than 1 \u03BCm. Statement I is correct.
Mycoplasma have no cell wall. Statement II is incorrect.`},{id:"neet-2022-q187",pn:187,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Monera and Protista",q:"Which of the following is a correct statement?",o:["Bacteria are exclusively heterotrophic organisms.","Slime moulds are saprophytic organisms classified under Kingdom Monera.","Mycoplasma have DNA, ribosome and cell wall.","Cyanobacteria are a group of autotrophic organisms classified under kingdom monera."],c:3,s:`Cyanobacteria are autotrophic and belong to kingdom Monera, so (4) is correct.
Bacteria can be autotrophic or heterotrophic.
Slime moulds belong to kingdom Protista.
Mycoplasma have no cell wall.`},{id:"neet-2021-q142",pn:142,y:"NEET 2021 \xB7 12 Sep",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Terms in classification",q:"Which of the following statements is correct ?",o:["Some of the organisms can fix atmospheric nitrogen in specialized cells called sheath cells","Fusion of two cells is called Karyogamy","Fusion of protoplasms between two motile on non-motile gametes is called plasmogamy","Organisms that depend on living plants are called saprophytes"],c:2,s:`Nitrogen is fixed in specialised cells called heterocysts, not sheath cells, so 1 is wrong.
Karyogamy is fusion of two nuclei, not cells, so 2 is wrong.
Plasmogamy is fusion of protoplasm of two gametes, so 3 is right.
Organisms living on living plants are parasites; saprophytes use dead matter, so 4 is wrong.`},{id:"neet-2020-q034",pn:34,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Viruses and viroids",q:"Which of the following is correct about viroids ?",o:["They have free RNA without protein coat.","They have DNA with protein coat.","They have free DNA without protein coat.","They have RNA with protein coat."],c:0,s:`Viroids are free RNA without a protein coat.
They are smaller than viruses.`},{id:"neet-2020-q041",pn:41,y:"NEET 2020 \xB7 13 Sep",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Unicellular algae",q:"Which of the following pairs is of unicellular algae?",o:["Gelidium and Gracilaria","Anabaena and Volvox","Chlorella and Spirulina","Laminaria and Sargassum"],c:2,s:`Chlorella is a unicellular green alga and Spirulina is a unicellular blue-green alga.
Gelidium, Gracilaria, Volvox, Laminaria and Sargassum are multicellular or colonial.`},{id:"neet-2019-q021",pn:21,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Viruses, viroids and prions",q:"Which of the following statements is incorrect ?",o:["Infective constituent in viruses is the protein coat","Prions consist of abnormally folded proteins","Viroids lack a protein coat","Viruses are obligate parasites"],c:0,s:`The infective part of a virus is its genetic material (DNA or RNA), not the protein coat.
So statement 1 is incorrect.`},{id:"neet-2019-q030",pn:30,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Kingdom Fungi",q:"Which of the following statement is incorrect ?",o:["Conidia are produced exogenously and ascospores endogenously.","Yeasts have filamentous bodies with long thread-like hyphae.","Morels and truffles are edible delicacies.","Clauiceps is a source of many alkaloids and LSD."],c:1,s:`Yeasts are single-celled and oval.
They do not form hyphae.
So statement 2 is incorrect.`},{id:"neet-2019-q070",pn:70,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Modes of nutrition and symbiosis",q:`Match Column-I with Column \u2013II.
Column-I: (a) Saprophyte (b) Parasite (c) Lichens (d) Mycorrhiza
Column-II: (i) Symbiotic association or fungi with plant roots (ii) Decomposition of dead organic materials (iii) Living on living plants of animals (iv) Symbiotic association of algae and fungi
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)","(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)","(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)","(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"],c:1,s:`A saprophyte feeds on dead organic matter.
A parasite lives on a living plant or animal.
A lichen is algae living with fungi.
Mycorrhiza is fungus living with plant roots.
So (a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i).`},{id:"neet-2018-q103",pn:103,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Prokaryotes and eukaryotes",q:"Which among the following is not a prokaryote ?",o:["Saccharomyces","Mycobacterium","Nostoc","Oscillatoria"],c:0,s:`Saccharomyces is yeast, a unicellular fungus, so it is eukaryotic.
Mycobacterium is a bacterium, and Nostoc and Oscillatoria are cyanobacteria; all are prokaryotes.`},{id:"neet-2018-q122",pn:122,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Five kingdoms",q:"Select the wrong statement :",o:["Cell wall is present in members of Fungi and Plantae.","Mushrooms belong to Basidiomycetes.","Pseudopodia are locomotory and feeding structures in Sporozoans.","Mitochondria are the powerhouse of the cell in all kingdoms excepts Monera."],c:2,s:`Cell walls occur in fungi and plants (1 true); mushrooms are basidiomycetes (2 true); Monera has no mitochondria (4 true).
Pseudopodia are used by amoeboid protozoans (sarcodines).
Sporozoans have no locomotory structures, so (3) is wrong.`},{id:"neet-2018-q128",pn:128,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Basidiomycetes",q:"After karyogamy followed by meiosis, spores are produced exogenously in -",o:["Neurospora","Alternaria","Agaricus","Saccharomyces"],c:2,s:`Basidiomycetes such as Agaricus make basidiospores exogenously on the basidium after karyogamy and meiosis.
Neurospora and Saccharomyces form ascospores inside an ascus (endogenously), and Alternaria has no sexual stage.`},{id:"neet-2018-q165",pn:165,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Diatoms",q:"Which of the following organisms are known as chief producers in the oceans?",o:["Dinoflagellates","Diatoms","Cyanobacteria","Euglenoids"],c:1,s:`Diatoms are the main photosynthetic organisms (phytoplankton) in the oceans.
They are called chief producers of the oceans.`},{id:"neet-2018-q167",pn:167,y:"NEET 2018 \xB7 6 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Ciliated protozoans",q:"Ciliates differ from all other protozoan in",o:["using flagella for locomotion","having a contractile vacuole for removing excess water","using pseudopodia for capturing prey","having two types of nuclei"],c:3,s:`Ciliates such as Paramecium have a macronucleus and a micronucleus.
Flagella and pseudopodia are used by other protozoans, and contractile vacuoles occur in other protozoans too.
So two types of nuclei is the difference.`},{id:"neet-2017-q060",pn:60,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Bacterial cell envelope",q:"Which of the following components provides sticky character to the bacterial cells ?",o:["Gylcocalyx","Cell wall","Nuclear membrane","Plasma membrane"],c:0,s:`The glycocalyx is the outermost layer of the bacterial envelope.
It is a slime layer or a thicker capsule of sticky polysaccharide.
It helps cells stick to surfaces. Bacteria have no nuclear membrane.`},{id:"neet-2017-q069",pn:69,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Archaebacteria",q:"Which of the following are found is extreme saline conditions ?",o:["Mycobacteria","Archaebacteria","Eubacteria","Cyanobacteria"],c:1,s:`Archaebacteria live in extreme habitats.
The halophiles are archaebacteria that live in very salty places.`},{id:"neet-2017-q071",pn:71,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Viruses and viroids",q:"Viroids differ from viruses in having",o:["RNA molecules without protein coat","DNA molecules with protein coat","DNA molecules without protein coat","RNA molecules with protein coat"],c:0,s:`Viroids are free low molecular weight RNA with no protein coat.
Viruses have a protein coat around their nucleic acid.`},{id:"neet-2017-q091",pn:91,y:"NEET 2017 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Biological Classification",st:"Mycoplasma",q:"Which among the following are the smallest living cells, known without a definite cell wall, pathogenic to plants as well as animals and can survive without oxygen ?",o:["Nostoc","Bacillus","Pseudomonas","Mycoplasma"],c:3,s:`Mycoplasmas are the smallest living cells and have no cell wall.
They can live without oxygen and cause disease in plants and animals.
Nostoc, Bacillus and Pseudomonas have cell walls.`}]})();
